<BaseLayout title="About | Steven Wager" description="From manufacturing to enterprise IT and software engineering education: Steven Wager's background, current practice, and learning direction.">
  <PageIntro label="ABOUT" title="Curiosity, put into practice." description="I’m Steven Wager—an enterprise IT professional, software engineering student, and someone who likes understanding how things work." />
  <section class="wrap about-layout"><aside class="profile-note"><span class="profile-initials" aria-hidden="true">SW<span>↗</span></span><h2>Steven Wager</h2><p>IT Support Specialist II<br />Software Engineering Student</p><div class="profile-line"><span class="eyebrow">MY THROUGH LINE</span><p>Understand the problem.<br />Build something useful.<br />Keep improving.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/resume">View professional résumé ↗</a></aside><div class="prose"><h2>From the shop floor to systems.</h2><p>My career began at Mercury Marine, where I spent seven years in manufacturing. As a Group Lead / Heat Treat Technician, I trained employees, worked with supervisors on production goals, and supported technical problem solving. A Lean Six Sigma Yellow Belt project gave me practical experience improving workstation ergonomics and reducing unnecessary movement.</p><p>In 2023, I joined Amcor and moved into enterprise IT. My work has included Microsoft 365, Active Directory, Microsoft Entra ID, endpoint administration, and technical operations. I now work as an IT Support Specialist II, supporting complex technical issues and collaborating with Information Security Operations.</p><h2>Building on that foundation.</h2><p>The work I enjoy most involves understanding a problem and making a process more reliable. I use Power Automate Desktop regularly and have created Microsoft Copilot agents at work. I also use PowerShell for practical automation. Those experiences connect my interests in software, infrastructure, and everyday operational improvements.</p><p>I’m pursuing a B.S. in Software Engineering at Western Governors University through the accelerated B.S. to M.S. pathway. Java is a primary programming interest, and I’m developing my skills through coursework and personal projects. React is part of my upcoming learning, not a professional specialization.</p><h2>What I’m exploring next.</h2><p>My current projects include Atlas, a PostgreSQL database project with Docker-based local development, and this Astro portfolio backed by a Cloudflare Worker. I’m also preparing for AWS certification and exploring infrastructure automation, homelab development, and container orchestration concepts.</p><p>My goal is to build a career in engineering-focused work while remaining grounded in the practical experience I already have. I value clear documentation, reliable systems, and learning through doing.</p></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE CURRENT TOOLKIT</p><h2>Practice and possibility.</h2></div></div><Toolkit /></section>
</BaseLayout>
